Subject: [PATCH] save: check the next chunk header is in range before reading
 it

SaveData_InitSubstructs ends a block with
    if (hdr[i].block != hdr[i + 1].block && i + 1 < gNumSaveChunkHeaders && ...)
At the last chunk the first operand reads hdr[gNumSaveChunkHeaders], one
entry past gSaveChunkHeaders. On the DS that address is the next bss object
and the read is harmless; on the host it is an out-of-bounds read and ASan
reports a global-buffer-overflow at boot (SaveData_New -> ...:762).

Put the bounds check first under SDK_PORT_3DS. The DS text is the original
order under #else; gcc-10 -E -P without SDK_PORT_3DS is byte-identical.

